00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.940
Hello Internet, welcome to Film Theory

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.960
where, just like a Lannister always

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:30.860
pays his debts,

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.640
a MatPat always delivers his theories.

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.580
In the crazy, ever changing, world of Game of Thrones

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:37.860
at least there are a few things

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:38.980
you can always count on.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.440
Winter is always coming,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.900
The Targaryens always have great hair,

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.420
and no one likes Dorne.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.620
seriously. *sounds of comments appearing* NOBODY likes Dorne.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:49.460
But if there's one thing I've learnt about this series

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:51.940
it's that you can't actually rely on anything.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.300
George R. R. Martin's love of throwing

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.480
fantasy tropes out the window

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.200
like a young Bran Stark

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.980
means that there is no assumption that you can count on.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.700
Which is why i'm so excited about this episode

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.600
as I finally get to target the family

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.360
that we all think we know, the Targaryens.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.860
In particular I've had my eye on the Mad King

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:11.140
for a long time now

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:14.380
and today we're going to talk about just how mad he is.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.340
Quick warning though, a light sprinkling of spoilers ahead

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.160
so I pray to the Old Gods that you're all caught up.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.300
Now, season 6 of the series was the first

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:24.280
we've gotten a look at the most famous

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.840
Targaryen ancestor, Aerys the second,

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.320
the Mad King himself.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.800
mmh, and what a looker he is.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.420
Now there are all kinds of theories going around

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.140
about the Mad King and there are

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:36.040
plenty of upcoming Film Theories about the fella.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.520
But today I'm less interested in history

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.520
and more interested in whether history

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.340
is going to repeat itself.

00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.080
Because for as excited as we all are

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.960
for Westeros to get rekt by Dany and her armies,

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.740
Dothraki hoards, ships and dragons

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.880
the biggest twist in her story may yet be coming.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.080
and sadly, nothing Sir Friend-Zone does

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.780
will be able to stop it.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:00.740
Nope. Dany may have a ticking bomb inside of her.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.780
Remember, the most famous family genes in

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:05.060
the whole series, the Targaryens,

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.440
i.e. the genes that let you walk through fire,

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.480
talk to dragons,

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.680
and make sure you always look

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.180
a Pantene Pro-V model

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:12.880
also tend to lead to rulers who

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:15.640
are violent, deranged and just weird.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.120
According to Game of Thrones cannon

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:20.120
Aerys the second was perfectly sane in his 20's

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:23.460
showing no signs he'd gotten the insane Targaryen gene

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:27.180
only to develop his homicidal crazies a little bit later in life.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.860
after becoming King.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:31.000
So is it just a matter of time for Daenerys as well?

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.960
Can science help us predict whether Dany is

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.920
destined to follow in her fathers footsteps?

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.100
I intend to find out.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:40.700
To figure it out, we need to take a look

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.320
at the Targaryen family tree

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.620
and boy is it a doozy!

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.320
Now in this show I usually try to stick

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.440
to the lore from the TV show only, since

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:51.120
at this point the two have taken different story arcs.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.440
For this one we needed to call out the big guns

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.020
to piece together Daenerys' genetic situation

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:59.000
and fully understand exactly what she's inheriting.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.980
Which means the lesson of todays episode

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.540
is the wonderful world of

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.500
Inbreeding [Children cheer]

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:05.740
and when I say 'wonderful'

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.040
i mean pretty weird.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.800
like, research for this episode was very uncomfortable

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.340
But to diagnose her likely-hood of

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.160
becoming the Mad Queen of Westeros,

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.700
we need to understand what happens

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.420
when related individuals do the horizontal mambo

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.940
and genetically why so many societies have rules

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.100
against marrying into your own family

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.380
other than the obvious creep factor

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.620
which again is pretty darn high

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:28.920
#love is love... most of the time.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:30.620
Now before Darwin and genetics,

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.820
people did know that inbreeding produced kids

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.560
that had physical and mental disabilities

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.360
who tended to die younger

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.120
or frankly didn't survive at all.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.240
But the reasons behind that have to do with

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:43.140
genetic science that came out in the 1800's

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.560
specifically, recessive genes and genetic mutation

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.660
and basically, how many are lurking

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.540
under the surface of our own genes everyday.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.540
So if you didn't sleep through 7th grade science

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.520
hopefully you know that every person in the world

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:57.740
has two copies of all their genes

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:59.240
one you inherit from your mum

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:00.700
and the other from your dad.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.920
In textbooks you see them sitting together

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.160
in these cute little pairs

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.920
all nice and getting along

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:09.020
But the story in your cells is a whole lot different.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:11.040
One of the biggest reasons we have two copies

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.600
of genes from two parents

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.160
is to cover up mutations and

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:16.160
alternate forms of genes in the genome

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:19.440
and what Mr Foster didn't tell me in 7th grade science

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.700
is that there are actually tons of these genetic mistakes

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.040
inside all of us.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:26.380
So if Gene 1 from your dad doesn't quite

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:27.320
have its act together

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.500
the one on the allele you got from your mum

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:30.860
can cover its tracks

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:33.340
making sure you still produce everything that you need

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.200
like blood cells and bones

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.800
and Kylie Jenner duck lips.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.040
Sometimes the traits these genes are for

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.460
are just unimportant like handedness

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.740
or the ability to taste certain bitter chemicals.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.580
But then there are other genes that you definitely

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:47.800
want to have a backup for.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.940
Diseases like Sickle Cell Anaemia and Cystic Fibrosis

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:52.500
are two of the most famous

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.380
autosomal recessive diseases, but there are

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:57.060
literally hundreds more

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:59.240
most of which you don't really hear too much about

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:00.860
because they're pretty darn rare

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:02.580
and the reason they're rare is that

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:04.300
most people have a backup set of genes

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:07.160
that help them minimise the effects of these disorders.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.560
Notice though that I said 'most'

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:12.280
If you don't have a backup set of genes

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:15.080
then boy-howdy you're in trouble

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:19.240
which brings us to Dany and her family history

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:20.640
of inbreeding

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:23.040
Inbreeding is actually really complicated

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:23.980
and what we're talking about here

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:25.540
just scratches the surface.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:27.480
Studying inbreeding is basically about

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.780
how many genes get recycled directly

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:31.480
from generation to generation.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.460
To do that, population specialists use what is known as

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:36.220
the coefficient of inbreeding.

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:38.300
gah, its like they make coefficients for

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.340
literally anything these days.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.240
Coefficient of when winter is coming.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:45.440
Coefficient of extraneous boob shots in Game of Thrones.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.900
But a coefficient of inbreeding measures how many

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:50.080
identical copies of a gene they have

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:52.100
because it came from the same ancestor.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.680
In other words, it helps us understand

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:56.360
how much of Daenerys' DNA is the exact same

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:59.140
as the Mad Kings because it came directly from him

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:00.880
and his inbreeding ancestors.

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.140
This, in turn, ought to give us a good indication

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:04.700
of whether we can expect Daenerys

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:06.500
to follow in the footsteps of his,

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:10.100
lets just say 'less than sane' ruling practices.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.820
Now, the equation for calculating

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:14.300
the inbreeding coefficient for any person is...

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:16.680
so.. right.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:19.400
Yeah, I'm gonna assume you don't want me to

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.200
walk through every variable on that one

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.920
so instead lets use the power of Google

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:25.060
to see what the inbreeding coefficient would be

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:27.160
for the children of two siblings.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:29.640
Using Google, and some weird research

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:30.720
into dairy cow breeding,

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.480
we can find that the sibling pairings will

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:35.100
will result in offspring that share 50%

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.160
of their genes with their grandparents

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:40.240
and have an inbreeding coefficient of 25%

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.980
Meaning that they have a 25% chance of

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:44.400
being effected by those nasty

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.800
recessive gene diseases we talked about.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.840
And the numbers are all well and good

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.520
but to put it in perspective lets look at

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:51.920
a real world example first.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:54.840
King Tutankhamun, known by his peeps as King Tut,

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:56.120
is one of the most famous cases

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.880
of real world inbreeding

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:00.420
since his parents were actually brother and sister.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.660
He's portrayed in Egyptian mythology as

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:04.980
this powerful sun god but in reality

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.160
he was really tiny,

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:07.880
likely sick his whole life,

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:09.280
had a congenital clubfoot,

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.940
couldn't produce any living children,

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:13.080
and died at age 19.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:15.120
Plus, he's the only child from his parents,

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:16.960
that we know, who actually survived.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.680
So what happened here?

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:20.960
Well, his grandparents weren't inbred.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:23.700
so first of a big pat on the back to those guys

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:25.800
for finding love in all the right places

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:29.800
[awkward, solo clapping]

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:32.020
His parents though, not so much

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:34.400
they were siblings, meaning that they already

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.360
share 50% of the same DNA

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:38.320
just by being closely related.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:39.580
now, they would have been fine

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:41.780
if they had gone on to have kids with other people

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:43.820
but they decided to keep it all in the family

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:46.680
meaning that any kid they had would be inbred

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.120
like, Really inbred.

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:50.580
When they had King Tut it meant that he had a

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:53.660
25% inbreeding coefficient because he's the product

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:54.600
of two siblings

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.860
versus say, a ZERO% coefficient if his parents

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:59.320
weren't actually related.

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:01.860
It also means that he shares 50% of his genes

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:03.240
with his grandparents

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:05.840
where he normally would only share 25%

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:08.140
of his genes with them under normal circumstances.

00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:10.400
As a result, his odds of getting any one of those

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:11.900
rare genetic diseases is now

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:14.000
as high as one in four.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.000
And across so many possible disorders

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.840
chances are you're going to end up with at least

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:18.820
a few of the biggies.

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:21.000
and thats the thing about the genetics of inbreeding

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.460
its all about percent chances

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:23.680
and playing the odds.

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:25.700
Kind of like Vegas but with your genes

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:28.620
Sure, you can definitely get lucky every once and a while

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:33.080
if having a club foot and dying by 19 is considered lucky,

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:35.700
but, statistically speaking, serious genetic mutations

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.380
become common as soon as you get to

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:39.680
a coefficient of inbreeding thats 10% or higher.

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:42.620
So what does this mean for Daenerys?

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.680
Well as you go through more and more

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:46.120
generations of inbreeding

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:49.520
the problems get worse and worse really fast

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:51.080
and say what you will about the Targeryens

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:53.860
but they were prolific inbreeders.

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:56.700
A little examination of that massive family tree

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:59.160
shows that you can go back 19 generations

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:01.660
from Daenerys and 12 of them have

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:03.760
sibling-sibling inbreeding involved.

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:05.480
Talk about your brotherly love!

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:07.300
actually don't talk about that, its gross

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:09.780
then again I'm still talking about it so..

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:11.380
Welcome to Film Theory ladies and gentlemen

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:15.260
So ok, lets give her the absolute biggest benefit of the doubt

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:17.320
and only go back three generations

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:19.040
to the last time there was any

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:21.600
ANY sort of out-breeding in the Targaryen line

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:22.980
Aegon 'The Unlikely'

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:24.880
Unlikely to survive based on the family's

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.140
incestuous history that is! ba-doom ching

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:30.140
Aegon 'The Unlikely' managed to marry Black Betha

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:32.300
a real, live non-Targaryen

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:35.340
oh, but okay sure. now its a race thing?

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:37.480
Seriously though, Black Betha's just her name

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:40.160
Now, Aegon the Unlikely also comes from inbreeding

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.340
but by marrying Betha and outcrossing

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:45.100
He effectively resets the Targaryen inbreeding

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.260
coefficient to zero.

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:49.060
According to the lore, Aegon didn't believe in inbreeding

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.540
but two of his kids fell in love and got married

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:55.260
bringing their kids, including Mad King Aerys the second

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:57.820
Up to that 25% inbreeding coefficient.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:00.320
As a result, it would be incredibly unlikely

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:01.960
that either Aerys or his sister

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.740
would live long enough to grow up

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.500
and they would almost certainly have

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.280
no chance of having viable kids.

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:09.820
An issue known as Inbreeding Depression.

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:12.140
No, thats not the feeling you get when your sister

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:14.000
starts having feelings for your first cousin.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.520
Thats actually when most populations become sterile

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:19.080
after one or two generations of close inbreeding

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:21.580
because their DNA is simply too damaged

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:23.020
to even create a baby.

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:25.700
But most importantly to us, the risk of Aerys having

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:28.500
Alzheimer's and Dementia, diseases that specifically

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:31.520
show up later in life, happen at much higher rates

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:33.040
in inbred populations.

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:35.460
More recessive genes mean more genes associated

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:38.020
Dementia and Alzheimers get turned on

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:40.220
leading to the diseases showing up more often

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:41.760
and more severely.

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:44.900
It also shows up earlier in life because inbreeding

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:47.840
causes the body to literally age faster

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:50.400
since its DNA is too fragile and literally

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.200
more likely to just break apart.

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:53.760
If you need a real life example,

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:56.580
just look at Maria of Portugal in the 1700's

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:59.080
whos life has some pretty bizarre similarities

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:00.500
to our favourite mad king.

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:02.280
The product of royal inbreeding,

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:05.840
she started off as a strong, decisive ruler early in life

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:08.800
until she started having delirious episodes

00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:10.040
and developing dementia.

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:11.840
Her condition got worse after the death

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:12.880
of her husband and son

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:15.380
and she lived the rest of her life in her own mind.

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:17.860
Those around her reported constantly hearing

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:20.000
her paranoid shrieking and screaming.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.480
As she was going mad, her kingdom was taken over

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:24.780
and the whole Portuguese royal family at the time

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:28.140
was forced to flee across the ocean to Brazil in 1801.

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:31.820
Historically, she's been refered to as the Mad Queen.

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:34.520
So what are Daenerys' odds of sharing the same fate

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:36.840
as her father and Maria of Portugal?

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:38.400
How do I put this lightly?

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:42.700
Really REALLY freaking high! Preposterously high!

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:45.920
Daenerys has 75% of her genes in common with

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:48.300
Viserys and her father Aerys the second

00:11:48.460 --> 00:11:50.100
Seventy-five percent!

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:52.840
That means that she's incredibly likely to

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:54.360
share the exact same fate as him.

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:56.880
When we hear Tyrion tell her she's starting to

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:58.300
sound a lot like her father

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:00.780
"You once told me you knew what your father was"

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:04.000
"Did you know his plans for Kings Landing when"

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.580
"the Lannister armies were at his gates?"

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:07.100
-"This is entirely different"

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:11.040
"You're talking about destroying cities, it's not entirely different"

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:14.220
It's because she literally is her father

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:16.740
three fourths of her, is her father

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:19.000
Physically, mentally, genetically

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.620
her fate is pretty well sealed

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:23.360
Man, it brings new meaning to

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:25.220
the idea of 'Daddy's little girl'

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:27.540
Now if you carry this out to its logical conclusion

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:30.040
it also has some serious implications for

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:31.340
her position as Queen.

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:33.780
The reason her first son died before he was born?

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:35.140
We think it was magic

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:36.580
We assume it was magic

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:39.460
But the much more likely explanation is that

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:42.480
she's too inbred to produce a living heir.

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:45.920
Based on genetics its practically impossible for her

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:46.960
to have a living offspring.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.840
and forget about marrying her.

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:50.600
Even if she makes it back to Westeros

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:52.780
and reclaims the Iron Throne for her family

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:55.440
statistically its almost impossible that she could

00:12:55.440 --> 00:12:57.000
extend her own family tree.

00:12:57.080 --> 00:13:00.360
There is literally no point in her becoming Queen

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:02.180
because there's so little chance that there

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:05.020
there will be anyone there to take it on after her.

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:06.740
well i guess there's always Cersei.

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:08.560
But if all this seems a bit extreme

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:10.920
if applying science to Game of Thrones seems

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:13.900
a bit absurd, you don't have to take my word for it.

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:16.820
Instead, take George R. R. Martin's word.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:19.540
In the epilogue of A Dance With Dragons

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:23.100
Mace Tyrell declares that Daenerys is quote:

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:25.540
"As mad as her father"

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:26.840
Just a throw away line?

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:30.340
or foreshadowing at whats to come once Daenerys

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:31.720
takes over Westeros?

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:33.420
We'll have to wait and see.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:35.540
Until then though, remember

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:37.360
Its just a theory.

